    hubIntro: 'Broome / Rubibi is a town-and-coast base; it is not a practical bed for every Kimberley excursion. Treat Cable Beach and Roebuck Bay as local choices, the Dampier Peninsula as a separately booked overnight, and the Gibb River Road as a multi-day expedition between the Derby and Kununurra ends. Kununurra and Purnululu need their own east-Kimberley block. These are separate operating areas, not a chain of nearby day trips.\n\nThe first decision is where you sleep after the last activity: a Broome town or Cable Beach address, an authorised peninsula property, a reserved station or park stay, or Kununurra. Then match each transfer to a real last mile. A town bus or hotel transfer can help around Broome; it does not reach a remote community, gorge, campground or private station. A map pin does not establish permission to enter Country, community land or a closed track.\n\nReviewed 13 October 2026. Main Roads WA explains that Gibb conditions change along the route and directs drivers to its live Travel Map and the separate Shire and parks reports. This review does not certify today’s road opening, river-crossing depth, fire rating, park access, tide window or community permission. If an official status cannot be confirmed for the exact segment, treat that segment as unavailable: do not infer an opening or use a side road as a workaround.',
