    hubIntro: 'Lutruwita / Tasmania rewards a route drawn around nights and gateways, not a fast-looking island loop. nipaluna / Hobart, kunanyi, the Tasman Peninsula, Launceston, Cradle Mountain and Freycinet occupy different operating systems: city walking, exposed alpine access, booked heritage entry, regional road transfer and weather-dependent park tracks. The five field guides ask which of those systems belongs on this trip and where the bed must be before the day begins. A place on a map is not a short hop; winding roads, daylight, wildlife, cold fronts and park closures decide whether two stops fit. Use the first morning and final connection as bookends: an early park start needs a nearby bed, while a late ferry or flight may need a separate Devonport, Hobart or Launceston night. When a road closure removes a leg, protect the arrival and return first, then drop one region; do not make a night drive the device that restores every pin.',
