        orientation: 'Cradle Mountain and Freycinet are not one park loop or a same-day pair. Cradle’s northern entrance is a remote alpine gateway; Freycinet is an east-coast peninsula with its own park pass, road, trailhead and coastal forecast. Use at least four nights for a brief two-park sampler: two nights at Cradle Valley and two in Coles Bay or another confirmed east-coast bed. That leaves one proper walk day per park and a separate transfer between the regions, but little weather margin. Six nights is more resilient: two at Cradle, one Launceston or transfer buffer, two at Coles Bay and one flexible night. Choose Cradle Valley lodging to reach the Visitor Centre and shuttle without an early cross-island drive; choose Coles Bay to reduce the Freycinet trailhead morning. A hotel in Launceston cannot serve as an easy daily base for both parks.',
